<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans";
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 15px; }
  th, td { padding: 8px; text-align: left; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; }
  th { font-weight: bold; }
</style>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="font-size: 20pt; text-align: center;">Colorado State University Department of Biochemistry</h1>
  <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; text-align: center;">BC 351-002 Principles of Biochemistry</h2>
  <p style="text-align: center; margin-top: 5px;">Fall Semester {{ current_year }}</p>

  <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
    <p>Instructor: <span data-field="instructor_name">{{ instructor_name }}</span></p>
    <p>Office: <span data-field="office_number">{{ office_number }}</span></p>
    <p>Phone: <span data-field="phone_number">{{ phone_number }}</span></p>
    <p>E-mail: <span data-field="email_address">{{ email_address }}</span></p>
    <p>Office Hours: {{ office_hours }}</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p>TA: <span data-field="ta_name">{{ ta_name }}</span></p>
    <p>Email: <span data-field="ta_email">{{ ta_email }}</span></p>
    <p>Study Sessions: <span data-field="study_sessions">{{ study_sessions }}</span></p>
    <p>Location: <span data-field="location">{{ location }}</span></p>
    <p>Schedule: {{ schedule }}</p>
    <p>Prerequisites: {{ prerequisites }}</p>
    <p>Textbook: <span data-field="textbook_info">{{ textbook_info }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Learning goals:</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><span data-field="learning_goal_1">{{ learning_goal_1 }}</span></li>
    <li><span data-field="learning_goal_2">{{ learning_goal_2 }}</span></li>
    <li><span data-field="learning_goal_3">{{ learning_goal_3 }}</span></li>
  </ol>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <p><strong>Canvas:</strong></p>
  <p>I will be using Canvas this semester in order to make available to you lecture notes, exam study materials, and lecture recordings. On Canvas, you will find the following:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>a. Course home page: When you login to this course this will be the default page.</li>
    <li>b. Announcements: I will make periodic announcements within Canvas to keep you abreast with the "happening" of the course.</li>
    <li>c. Modules: There are 19 modules in this class. The 1st module is the syllabus module that contains:
      <ol>
        <li>Syllabus and Course schedule</li>
        <li>Ebook introductory recording</li>
        <li>How to use the ebook's grade book</li>
        <li>Student Guide to Polleverywhere</li>
        <li>Recitation topics</li>
        <li>Link to the textbook</li>
      </ol>
      There are 14 modules that correspond directly to a chapter within the book. In each of these modules you will find:
      <ol>
        <li>A PowerPoint file for the module's set of lectures.</li>
        <li>There are 4 exam study materials modules:
          <ol>
            <li>These modules contain: study guides, practice exams, learning objectives. They are found immediately following the last chapter for that particular exam.</li>
          </ol>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </li>
    <li>d. Grades:</li>
    <li>e. Echo360</li>
    <li>f. Media Gallery: This page contains media (mostly Youtube videos) that I have spent time researching and feel they will help you understand the material.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Attendance:</h3>
  <p><span data-field="attendance_policy">{{ attendance_policy }}</span></p>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Exam Attendance:</h3>
  <p><span data-field="exam_attendance_policy">{{ exam_attendance_policy }}</span></p>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">SDC arrangements:</h3>
  <p><span data-field="sdc_arrangements">{{ sdc_arrangements }}</span></p>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Assignments:</h3>
  <p>This class consists of 14-chapter quizzes (5 points each), 4 exams (100 points each), and 14 metacognition questions (15 points total) as detailed below:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Chapter Quizzes – 70 points
      <p>These will be presented through the book. There will be a total of {{ quiz_count }} quizzes equaling 70 points. You will have two opportunities to take the quizzes. Your highest score of the two attempts will be recorded. Due dates for the final attempt on each quiz are listed on the schedule.</p>
    </li>
    <li>Metacognition Questions – 15 points
      <p>These will be presented in the book in the "Metacognition Questions" tab. Each chapter will have a single question worth 1 point each. There are no "right" or "wrong" answers for these questions, but you will need to do them and take them seriously to receive credit for them. Due dates for each question are listed on the schedule.</p>
    </li>
    <li>Glycolysis Drag-n-drop assignment – 15 points
      <p>This assignment will be presented in the book in Chapter 11. As the time approaches I will address how and when to complete this assignment.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Exams – 400 points</h3>
  <p>I am going to give four exams. Each one will worth 100 points.</p>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">How to Study:</h3>
  <p><span data-field="study_advice">{{ study_advice }}</span></p>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Grades:</h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Grade</th>
        <th>Percentage</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>A+</td>
        <td>97-100%</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>A</td>
        <td>90 - &lt; 97%</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>B+</td>
        <td>87 - &lt; 90%</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>B</td>
        <td>80 - &lt; 87%</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>C+</td>
        <td>77 - &lt; 80%</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>C</td>
        <td>70 - &lt; 77%</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>D</td>
        <td>60 - &lt; 70%</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>F</td>
        <td>below 60%</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Grade Breakdown:</h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Assignment</th>
        <th>Points Counted</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>4 Exams (100 points each)</td>
        <td>400</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Metacognition questions</td>
        <td>15</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Glycolysis drag-n-drop</td>
        <td>15</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>14 Quizzes (5 points each)</td>
        <td>70</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Total</td>
        <td>500</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Extra Credit:</h3>
  <p><span data-field="extra_credit_policy">{{ extra_credit_policy }}</span></p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Lecture Schedule</h3>
  <h4 style="text-align: center;">SUBJECT TO CHANGE</h4>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>DATE</th>
        <th>DAY</th>
        <th>TOPIC</th>
        <th>TEXT</th>
        <th>QUIZ (DUE DATE)</th>
        <th>METACOG (DUE DATE)</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for lecture in lecture_schedule %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ lecture.date }}</td>
        <td>{{ lecture.day }}</td>
        <td>{{ lecture.topic }}</td>
        <td>{{ lecture.text }}</td>
        <td>{{ lecture.quiz_info }}</td>
        <td>{{ lecture.metacog_info }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>